1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
Uber does not own the cars, kitchens, or

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:04,800
the freight it moves; it owns the network

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:05,600
that connects them.

4
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,500
Riders open the app, drivers use their own

5
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:10,800
cars, and every completed trip is matched by

6
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:11,400
the platform.

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,100
Uber takes a service fee from every fare;

8
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,200
the driver keeps the rest, and the platform

9
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:17,000
keeps the match.

10
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,200
The app sells delivery, freight, advertising and memberships,

11
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,700
so one network earns in more than one

12
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:23,300
way.

13
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:26,000
More riders make each car busier, more drivers

14
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,300
shorten the wait, and the network gets harder

15
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:28,900
to leave.
